    "durationMs": 170461,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified — `sh start.sh` applies Knex migrations and serves on `0.0.0.0:8000` (confirmed bound to `00000000` in procfs), and the database is left empty for the test suite.\n\nImplementation summary:\n- **Stack**: Express 4.21 on Node 22, Knex + `pg` (idiomatic query builder with migrations), all DB settings read from `DATABASE_URL`\n- **Endpoints**: `POST /links` (201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, URLs returned unchanged, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 for missing/invalid url, invalid codes, malformed JSON), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 with atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING` so clicks increment exactly once), `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `total`)\n- **Codes**: 4–20 ASCII letters/digits/hyphens/underscores validated; omitted codes are 6-char crypto-random with collision retry\n- **Persistence**: single `links` table via migration; verified links and click counts survive a full server restart\n- **Files**: `src/app.js`, `src/server.js`, `src/db.js`, `migrations/`, `scripts/migrate.js`, `start.sh`, `README.md` (with start instructions), `.gitignore`"
  }
